+## Renaming / updating a local entry
+
+The layer used to be create-and-delete only: changing one field meant demote +
+re-promote, and a slug shadowed by a newly shipped curated one (marked in the
+`switch.sh --list` footer) advertised a rename that did not exist. Now:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/catalog.sh rename --slug <engine>/<name> --to <engine>/<new-name>
+bash scripts/catalog.sh update --slug <engine>/<name> --set status=production
+bash scripts/catalog.sh update --slug <engine>/<name> --set max_ctx=262144 --set tp=2
+```
+
+Both change ONLY `registry.local.json` here — no profile, compose, or engine
+file moves. `--dry-run` validates and previews without writing; `--root DIR`
+targets a throwaway tree. Rules: `origin` is not editable (the loader stamps
+`"local"`), an entry's `engine` must equal its slug's namespace (to move it
+under another engine, rename), and a rename refuses curated slugs in both
+directions plus any target engine the profile layer does not know. After any
+amend the layer must still load through `compose_registry.load_local_registry`
+— a change that would not is refused before anything is written.
+
